# L §5.11: "Over a binding that is empty at the cut and whose span reaches past it, first and last give a hole naming
# the binding (HOLE-NOTYET), since a member may still come (§3.1, P-9); any other empty first or last is refused
# (RUN-EMPTY)"; L §8.1 HOLE-NOTYET "<x>: no <event> yet, and its span reaches past the cut" (writer 8: x is the
# binding's variable, event its domain); "Over things ... without [ties by] they are refused", empty or not, at load
# (round 18 C1-14; writer 8 moved q1 to L5_11_first_no_ties_load). Nobody in persons is retired: over 2026 (past the cut 2026-06-30) q3 is HOLE-NOTYET; over 2026-Q1 (before the
# cut) q2 is RUN-EMPTY; L §8.1's fix "tests count(...) > 0 first" gives false (q4). (Was pending, removed.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
kind persons
input retired[p in persons]: bool

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ana] lives 1990-01-01..
  retired[ana] = false

ask q2: first(p in persons over 2026-01-01 .. 2026-03-31 where retired[p]) ties by lifespan(p).from
ask q3: last(p in persons over 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 where retired[p]) ties by lifespan(p).from
ask q4: count(p in persons over 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 where retired[p]) > 0
=== expect
q2: refused: RUN-EMPTY ...
  cut 2026-06-30
q3: ?"p: no persons yet, and its span reaches past the cut" (persons)
  cut 2026-06-30
q4: false
  cut 2026-06-30
